{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Stack pushed. Both mechanisms are now up for review:\n\n- change 1717 ps3 — \"Sweep compaction out of band on a schedule\" (commit 3cfde6b8f3), the\n  amortized path where CI exists.\n- change 1727 — \"Trigger compaction from the close, out of band\" (commit f34549d099), the\n  operation-linked floor that works with no CI and no cron.\n\nStacked deliberately rather than folded into one patch set: different blast radii, different\ntests, and the reviewer gets two units instead of one lump. 1727 sits on 1717, so submitting\nthe top submits its ancestor.\n\nRebased onto current main first, which brought in two commits that matter here:\n- 6601e5fb21 \"Guard caplog on the reconciler root too\" — the fix for the order-dependent\n  reconciler test that -1'd my last two patch sets. It landing confirms the triage I recorded\n  was right on the MECHANISM, not just the outcome: I argued logger propagation rather than the\n  `declined` counter, and cross-directory state rather than anything in that suite.\n- 641ba8bed1 \"Split event_append by concern into three modules\" — which is why I re-ran both\n  tiers on the rebased stack rather than trusting the pre-rebase runs.\n\nFinal local verification on the exact pushed tree:\n- main tier (CI's invocation): 12772 passed, 52 skipped, 0 failed.\n- integration tier: re-running now. My last amend touched only comment text in\n  `_config_schema.py` and a unit-test rewrite, neither of which is on an integration path, and\n  the main tier covers all of tests/interfaces — but this tier has held the only real failure\n  twice in this ticket, so I am not calling it green until it says so.\n- gates: ruff, mypy (526 files), complexity ratchet unchanged, module-size contract, all five\n  generators with zero diff, actionlint + zizmor clean on the workflow."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786620195810849001,"uuid":"1db639b2-15ef-4999-9c56-2889c1fcd70e"}